@startuml activity-approve-or-reject
' Spec 004 — approving and rejecting a waiting listing (REQ-004-5, -6)
title Approve or reject (REQ-004-5/6)

start
:Admin has read a listing that
is Waiting for approval;
if (Decision?) then (approve)
  if (Still Pending approval?) then (no)
    :Refuse — "This listing is no longer
    waiting for approval." Nothing changes;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (Its region is active?) then (no)
    :Refuse — the region is hidden. Suggest:
    show the region again, change the region
    (Edit), or reject with a reason.
    The page reloads and shows the flag;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Status → Published;
  :Record the time and the Admin;
  note right
    The listing's content is not changed.
    An Admin may approve their own listing.
    The free-tier limit is not checked:
    a waiting listing already counts as open.
    The approval time is the "posted" date (005).
  end note
  :Email the employer (REQ-004-9);
  :Back to the queue with a confirmation;
  stop
else (reject)
  :Admin writes what needs to change.
  The form says "The employer will see this.";
  if (Still Pending approval?) then (no)
    :Refuse — "This listing is no longer
    waiting for approval." Nothing changes;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (Reason is 10–500 characters?) then (no)
    :Validation error — stays
    Pending approval;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Status → Rejected, reason saved.
  The employer sees "Needs changes" and the reason;
  :Record the time and the Admin;
  :Frees one open-listing slot (003);
  :Email the employer the reason (REQ-004-9);
  :Back to the queue with a confirmation;
  stop
endif
@enduml
